<title>UK: Rank up as old bid rumours resurface.</title>
<headline>Rank up as old bid rumours resurface.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Rank Group Plc climbed to a four-and-a-half month high on Friday as old bid rumours resufurced, dealers said.</p>
<p>By 1151 GMT, the shares were up 11p to 446-1/2 on turnover of 3.2 million shares.  </p>
<p>Dealers said vague bid rumours bolstered the shares, but some discounted the talk, saying the shares were due for a bounce anyway.</p>
<p>&quot;They've been massive underperformers,&quot; said one dealer.</p>
<p>Rank declined to comment on the bid talk.</p>
<p>--London newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
